  <tr><td>Arrest memo</td><td>Sequence relative to FIR and recovery; compliance with arrest safeguards</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Sampling record</td><td>Compliance with the statutory inventory-and-sampling procedure before a Magistrate under Section 52A</td></tr>
  <tr><td>FSL trail</td><td>Integrity of seals and deposit timeline between seizure and laboratory</td></tr>
</table>
<div class="note">Quantity classification drives NDPS bail: small-quantity cases attract liberal consideration, commercial-quantity cases attract Section 37&rsquo;s twin conditions, and intermediate cases — like this one — turn on ordinary bail principles sharpened by the quality of the investigation. Nothing in a bail order forecasts the trial&rsquo;s outcome.</div>
